<h2>Direct Upload Progress</h2>
<p>Show a progress bar for each file as it uploads via Rails ActiveStorage direct uploads.</p>

<p>
  This app has no database (<code>--skip-active-record</code>), so there's no
  real ActiveStorage to upload to. The file input below is wired to a
  demo-only <code>demo-direct-upload</code> controller that dispatches the
  same <code>direct-upload:*</code> events ActiveStorage's own JS would
  dispatch on a real upload, on a fake timer, so you can see
  direct-upload-progress render without a backend. Pick a file whose name
  contains "fail" (e.g. <code>fail.txt</code>) to see the error state.
</p>

<div class="demo-box" data-controller="demo-direct-upload direct-upload-progress">
  <label for="attachments">Attachments</label>
  <input
    id="attachments"
    type="file"
    multiple
    data-demo-direct-upload-target="input"
    data-action="
      change->demo-direct-upload#start
      direct-upload:initialize->direct-upload-progress#add
      direct-upload:progress->direct-upload-progress#progress
      direct-upload:error->direct-upload-progress#error
      direct-upload:end->direct-upload-progress#end
    "
  />

  <ul data-direct-upload-progress-target="list"></ul>
  <p data-direct-upload-progress-target="status"></p>
</div>
